WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:05.880
Let’s talk about what’s happening in India.

00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:12.120
It has to do with these protests. They started late last year.

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:25.200
More than 50 people were killed. Hindus and Muslims.

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:31.560
Since then Delhi Police have been detaining and questioning hundreds of people about those protests.

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:37.560
But a report by Amnesty International accuses those same police of taking part in the violence.

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:39.880
So what’s going on with these arrests? 

00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:42.800
Why is a citizenship law causing so much anger? 

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:47.920
And why are some people worried about what this means for India as a secular country?

00:00:56.240 --> 00:00:59.360
India’s going through a tough time.

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:05.200
Millions of people have been infected with COVID-19 and the economy has shrunk dramatically.

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:10.280
And on top of that there are a lot of unresolved issues that date back to those protests.

00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:13.800
It’s all about identity and what it means to be Indian.

00:01:16.120 --> 00:01:21.640
India has almost 1.4 billion people. About 80% of them are Hindu.

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:25.000
But the minorities are still huge — in the millions. 

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:29.760
Muslims, Christians, Sikhs. Plus immigrants from neighbouring countries.

00:01:31.960 --> 00:01:39.080
Now under India’s secular constitution everyone is guaranteed equal rights — regardless of their religion.

00:01:39.080 --> 00:01:48.160
But right now a lot of people say that equality is being threatened, that the ruling party, the BJP, has an agenda to make India a Hindu nation.

00:01:48.160 --> 00:01:53.800
They say the latest sign of that is a law passed in December called the Citizenship Amendment Act.

00:01:53.800 --> 00:02:00.200
The Act offers a pathway to becoming an Indian citizen for migrants who arrived before 2015

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:03.760
from these countries and who belong to these religions.

00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:06.240
Muslims aren’t on the list.

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:10.960
But the BJP says it’s because they’re not a persecuted minority in those three countries.

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:15.000
The law they say is meant to help those at risk.

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:25.320
But critics have been saying that if the CAA is there to offer citizenship to persecuted minorities

00:02:33.680 --> 00:02:39.760
But critics have been saying that if the CAA is there to offer citizenship to persecuted minorities

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:42.600
there are plenty of Muslim minorities in that position.

00:02:54.080 --> 00:02:57.200
But the CAA alone isn’t the problem.

00:02:57.200 --> 00:03:03.320
It’s the combination of the Act with a National Register of Citizens that India wants to introduce.

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:05.520
It’s basically a massive headcount.

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:06.720
So here’s the issue.

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:10.400
To register people have to prove that they’re Indian citizens.

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:14.200
But not everyone can. Not everyone has the documents.

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:23.080
There’s concern that immigrants could be granted citizenship under the CAA while Muslims who are actually from India could be left out.

00:03:25.520 --> 00:03:26.680
Here’s one scenario.

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:31.200
Let’s say this person was born in India where generations of his family are from.

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:33.760
He’s Muslim. We’ll call him Abid.

00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:38.120
Then there’s Suranjit. He came to India seven years ago from Bangladesh.

00:03:38.120 --> 00:03:39.360
He’s Hindu.

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:42.600
Neither of them have the documents to prove where they’re from.

00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:48.240
Abid can’t apply for citizenship under the CAA because it doesn’t mention Muslims.

00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:51.240
But Suranjit stands a chance because he’s Hindu.

00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:05.960
And this goes beyond the hypothetical.

00:04:05.960 --> 00:04:10.000
The state of Assam tried to register people and it didn’t go well.

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:15.240
Nearly 2 million people — including Muslims and Hindus — didn’t qualify.

00:04:23.160 --> 00:04:27.400
The government is forging ahead with the CAA and the register anyway. 

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:30.560
But people aren’t just worried about it not working.

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:34.760
Many Muslims say it’s just another example of injustice.

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:40.480
In 1992 Hindu nationalists destroyed the Babri mosque.

00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:46.040
There were riots and nearly 2,000 people were killed.

00:04:46.040 --> 00:04:50.360
Nationalist groups as well as BJP leaders were linked to the violence.

00:04:53.240 --> 00:05:00.840
Ten years later in Gujarat fighting between Muslims and Hindus ended in a thousand people dead. Most of them Muslims.

00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:06.400
At the time the current prime minister, Narendra Modi, was chief minister there.

00:05:06.400 --> 00:05:09.680
He was accused of deliberately allowing the riots to happen.

00:05:31.880 --> 00:05:37.120
So it’s off the back of that history that the BJP brought in the CAA.

00:05:40.600 --> 00:05:46.200
It wasn’t just Muslims protesting. Plenty of Indians from other faiths were against it too.

00:06:01.240 --> 00:06:08.720
There were also rallies in favour of the CAA where BJP politicians spoke to the crowds.

00:06:30.760 --> 00:06:35.320
Protesters started getting attacked. Then both sides started fighting.

00:06:40.200 --> 00:06:43.200
Hindus attacked Muslims. Muslims fought back.

00:06:50.800 --> 00:06:56.720
Muslims and Hindus were killed. But it was mostly Muslims.

00:07:06.520 --> 00:07:13.080
The BJP and its supporters have dismissed accusations that Muslim protesters suffered disproportionately.

00:07:13.080 --> 00:07:18.360
They also deny using hate speech that might’ve fuelled violence by Hindu nationalists.

00:07:37.520 --> 00:07:37.560
But a report by Amnesty International says some Delhi Police were complicit in the violence.

00:07:37.920 --> 00:07:43.480
But a report by Amnesty International says some Delhi Police were complicit in the violence.

00:07:51.840 --> 00:07:55.240
They’ve also been accused of actively taking part.

00:08:06.160 --> 00:08:11.680
Delhi Police didn’t respond to Al Jazeera’s requests for an interview after the Amnesty report came out.

00:08:12.160 --> 00:08:14.840
But the government says the rights group is biased.

00:08:23.360 --> 00:08:28.200
Meanwhile Delhi Police have been questioning, arresting and detaining hundreds of people.

00:08:28.720 --> 00:08:31.560
Some of them under an anti-terror law.

00:08:31.560 --> 00:08:38.240
Rights activists in India say that more than 800 Muslims have been picked up,
that it’s being misused to crack down

00:08:38.240 --> 00:08:42.840
on political dissent and that police have used the pandemic to clampdown.

00:08:42.840 --> 00:08:48.480
Professor Apoorvanand, who we heard from earlier, was one of the people taken in for questioning.

00:09:02.640 --> 00:09:02.760
It’s all causing a lot of fear and mistrust.

00:09:08.800 --> 00:09:12.880
It’s all causing a lot of fear and mistrust.

00:09:43.400 --> 00:09:50.040
It all comes back to the idea of identity and a lot of people feeling powerless and excluded.

00:09:50.040 --> 00:09:55.480
They want to know who gets to be Indian. And who gets to decide.

